  "raw_label": "appellant_won",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Rafeeq.C. S vs State Of Kerala on 24 December, 2024 2024:Ker:97782 B.A.No.10156 of 2024 1 In The High Court Of Kerala At Ernakulam Present The Honourable Mrs. Justice M.B. Snehalatha Tuesday, The 24Th Day Of December 2024 / 3Rd Pousha, 1946 Bail Appl. No. 10156 Of 2024 Crime No.473/2024 Of Kaipamangalam Police Station, Thrissur, Thrissur Petitioner: 1 Rafeeq.C. S., Aged 51 Years C/O. Shamsudeen, Chaminiyil House, Near Mahlara, Kaipamangalam.P.O., Thrissur Dist., Pin - 680681 2 Asfer.C. A, Aged 44 Years, S/O. Aliyar.C.B., Chirakuzhi House, P.O. Ponjanam, Kattur, Thrissur Dist., Pin - 680702 By Advs. Sri.Jithin Babu A Sri.Azeem Salih Sri.Arun Samuel Sri.Anood Jalal K.J. Respondent: State Of Kerala, Represented By Public Prosecutor, High Court Of Kerala, Pin - 682031 BY ADV. SMT.T.V. NEEMA-SR.GP THIS BAIL APPLICATION HAVING COME UP FOR ADMISSION ON 24.12.2024, THE COURT ON THE SAME DAY DELIVERED THE FOLLOWING: 2024:KER:97782 Rafeeq.C. S vs State Of Kerala on 24 December, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/188672437/ 1 B.A.No.10156 of 2024 2 M.B.SNEHALATHA, J ------------------------------------------- B.A. No.10156 of 2024 --------------------------------------------- Dated this the 24th day of December, 2024 ORDER This Bail Application is filed under Section 483 of the Bharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita (BNSS), 2023. 2.",
    "facts": "The above case is registered against the petitioners alleging offences punishable under Sections 273, 304 r/w 34 of IPC and Section 118(e) of the Kerala Police Act. The petitioners/accused along with other accused were running a hotel named 'Zain' at Perinjanam without adhering to food safety measures. The accused persons, in furtherance of their common intention, sold stale and adulterated food to their customers and due to the consumption of food from the said hotel, defacto complainant's sister Usaiba died of the food poisoning. Earlier, the petitioners had field an application for bail under Section 438 of the Cr.P.C. seeking pre-arrest bail and this Court dismissed the same with a direction to surrender before the investigating Officer.",
    "arguments": "The learned counsel for the petitioners/accused would contend that, petitioners are innocent; that they have not committed any crime as alleged."
  },
